\section{Discussion and Conclusion}
\label{sec:conclusion}

The belief that RLVR is inherently superior to SFT for recovering pruned reasoning models turns out to depend on how the model was pruned.
Under diversity-preserving pruning, the two paradigms produce near-identical accuracy (mean $|\Delta| {=} 0.54$\,pp across four fine-grained criteria at 20\%; max $1.34$\,pp including dose-response and MBPP), yet the pruning criterion itself creates a 4.4$\times$ gap in peak reward between CKA-only and Standard---a gap that persists through 300 training steps (\S\ref{sec:extended_analysis}).
Representational diversity predicts this recovery capacity: CKA-only diverges most from the dense representation ($\mu{=}0.62$) yet recovers best, while collapsing methods preserve dense fidelity ($\mu{\geq}0.88$).

\paragraph{Why does diversity preservation enable RL recovery?}
Policy gradient methods require trajectory variation to estimate reward gradients; importance-based pruning collapses the model onto the dense model's dominant reasoning mode, while CKA-only pruning preserves representationally distinct pathways that sustain exploration.
Gradient flow evidence supports this: CKA-only exhibits 2.89$\times$ mean gradient magnitude vs.\ Standard (\S\ref{sec:extended_analysis}), consistent with diversity preventing zero-variance batches ($f_0 > 0.5$).
Since RL fine-tuning updates only 5--30\% of parameters~\citep{mukherjee2025rlsubnetworks}, CKA-based pruning may preferentially preserve this active subnetwork---a recovery analogue of the Lottery Ticket Hypothesis~\citep{frankle2019lth}---though decoupling shows accuracy is paradigm-invariant.

\paragraph{Practitioner guidelines.}
Prefer CKA-only or high-$\alpha$ \rasp{} ($\alpha \geq 2.0$); the inverted-U (Figure~\ref{fig:dose_response}) confirms moderate diversity weighting outperforms both extremes.
Under SFT alone, the criterion still matters (4.62\,pp gap; Table~\ref{tab:decoupling}).
Maintain per-layer floors ($\geq$40\%), stay below 25\% sparsity (\S\ref{sec:sparsity_cliff}), and monitor early-step $f_0$ as a pruning quality diagnostic.

\paragraph{Scope and outlook.}
Reward-accuracy decoupling holds across all tested sparsity levels ($|\Delta| \leq 1$\,pp at 15--25\%), with initial generality evidence across scales (1.5B) and architectures (Qwen2.5-Math-7B).
Our findings concern fine-grained structural pruning; extension to unstructured~\citep{selfhealing2025} or online rollout pruning~\citep{xu2026arrol} remains open. Code, pruning masks, and model checkpoints will be released upon acceptance.
